<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tansen, Nepal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tansen">Tansen</a> is a hill town in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, the headquarters of Palpa District, on a ridge of the Mahabharat range. From the 16th century it was the capital of the Sen kings of Palpa, once the strongest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaubise-rajya">Chaubise Rajya</a>, until its annexation by the Gorkha kingdom in 1806. Newar traders settled there, and its temples and Tansen Durbar palace reflect that history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tansen-nepal.jpg" alt="Tansen, Nepal" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mithunkunwar9 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Evening_View_of_Tansen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
